<h2><a name="_description"></a>DESCRIPTION <a href="#_top"><img alt="^" border="0" src="../../up.png"></a></h2>
<div class="fragment"><pre class="comment">CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI M-file for CalibrateSolenoidGUI.fig
      CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI, by itself, creates a new CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI or raises the existing
      singleton*.

      H = CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI returns the handle to a new CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI or the handle to
      the existing singleton*.

      CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI('Property','Value',...) creates a new CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI using the
      given property value pairs. Unrecognized properties are passed via
      varargin to CalibrateSolenoidGUI_OpeningFcn.  This calling syntax produces a
      warning when there is an existing singleton*.

      CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI('CALLBACK') and CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI('CALLBACK',hObject,...) call the
      local function named CALLBACK in CALIBRATESOLENOIDGUI.M with the given input
      arguments.

      *See GUI Options on GUIDE's Tools menu.  Choose &quot;GUI allows only one
      instance to run (singleton)&quot;.

 See also: GUIDE, GUIDATA, GUIHANDLES</pre></div>

